   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "CHARACTER EDIT -- Qwen-Image-Edit 2509\n\nLoad the image to change in LoadImage, then say what to change in the\nTextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus 'prompt' box -- an instruction, not a\ndescription: \"replace the left pauldron with a glass chamber of green\nfluid\", not \"a figure with a glass pauldron\".\n\nDenoise is a cliff, not a slider.  Below about 0.75 nothing moves;\nabove it the whole figure is redrawn.  If the edit will not take, it is\nusually the prompt, not the number.\n\n---\n\nQwen-Image-Edit 2509 (Apache-2.0): change part of an existing\nconcept instead of rerolling the whole thing. Use this when a\ndesign is approved except for one element - swapping a pauldron,\nchanging a colour, removing a prop - because a regeneration,\neven on the same seed, will not preserve the rest. Phrase the\nprompt as an instruction and say what to KEEP: 'Replace X with\nY, keeping everything else identical.' FluxKontextImageScale\nsnaps the input to a resolution the model was trained on. 20\nsteps at cfg 4.0 rather than the 4-step Lightning LoRA on\npurpose: applying a bf16 LoRA to the fp8 base makes ComfyUI\ndequantize to patch it, and that spike OOMs a 16GB card - the\nsame wall txt2img_qwen_fast.json works around with a pre-merged\ncheckpoint, which does not exist for the edit model. DENOISE IS\nTHE STYLE KNOB. At the default 1.0 the whole image is re-\ndiffused and the model's own style prior wins: asking to\n'simplify' a painted illustration returns flat vector art or\nfeatureless clay no matter how many times the prompt says 'not\ncartoon'. Lower it to preserve the source's rendering while\nstill applying the edit: ~0.8 for a small swap, ~0.5-0.65 to\nrestyle or simplify while keeping the painterly surface. Reach\nfor this before adding more words to the prompt."
   ],
